# Drafted by Gemini (side quests act 2 batch 1: letter), edited.

~ effects
Narrator: A cedar shelf holds a dead traveler's belongings: a brass button, dry boots, and a folded letter sealed with tallow.
mori_shade [sad]: Walder Pye came in on the rain cart and never rose again. That letter was dry inside his coat, waiting for someone with living feet.
* Take the letter -> take
* Leave -> END

~ take
mori_shade [weary]: It is addressed to his kin past the border stones. Carry it past the gate yourself, if you please, for our post office cannot leave a dead man's final words untouched.
give walder_letter
quest walders_letter asked
set letter_asked
-> END

~ counter
Narrator: Ink pots stand in neat brass rows along the counter, smelling of vinegar and damp feathers.
theodora_mayville [neutral]: Step up to the grate and declare your parcels. No written matter leaves Wickermoor during the quarantine without my stamp and inspection.
* [ends:walders_letter] Hand it over -> hand
* [Sleight of Hand DC 13] Keep it hidden -> slip_ok | slip_caught
* [Deception DC 11] Say you have nothing to post -> nothing_ok | slip_caught

~ hand
theodora_mayville [sly]: How wise of you to trust the proper channels. Poor Walder's penmanship is dreadful, and his gloom would only upset his folk, so I shall improve it before the bag goes out.
set letter_outcome = "seized"
quest walders_letter lost
-> END

~ slip_ok
Narrator: `{name}` slides the tallow-sealed paper beneath a cuff just as the postmaster peers over her spectacles.
theodora_mayville [neutral]: Empty hands and loitering boots. If you have no business with the post, clear the counter for those who can read a notice.
-> END

~ nothing_ok
theodora_mayville [weary]: Then do not breathe upon my brasswork. Stand aside and keep your hands where the parish can see them.
-> END

~ slip_caught
theodora_mayville [angry]: Unstamped correspondence concealed in a coat! Constable Squire, take these smugglers to the cells while I correct this wretched letter's tone.
doris_squire [neutral]: In the irons till morning, the lot of you. Move your feet.
jail wickermoor_constable_station:cells until days_since.jailed >= 1
-> END

~ hilda
Narrator: Hilda tightens a leather girth strap by the moor road, her oilskin cloak smelling of wet heather and woodsmoke.
hilda_brom [neutral]: Heading past the boundary stones before the fog thickens. Speak quick if you want something.
* Give her the letter to carry -> hilda_take
* Leave -> END

~ hilda_take
hilda_brom [smile]: Walder Pye's hand. He paid his tab and kept his dog quiet, so I will ride this out in my dry pack and drop it with the border carrier.
set letter_outcome = "sent"
quest walders_letter done
gold +15
-> END
